<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3" title="In 3.3 Case 2: General Case with Aleatory Uncertainty in 𝐗 (X is random) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ System-Level Uncertainty Quantification with Multiple Machine Learning Models: A Theoretical Framework" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Transformation of Model Uncertainty Variables (<math class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#S3.SS3.SSS1" title="In 3.3 Case 2: General Case with Aleatory Uncertainty in 𝐗 (X is random) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ System-Level Uncertainty Quantification with Multiple Machine Learning Models: A Theoretical Framework" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">3.3.1 </span>Unified Independent Space and Final Expression</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsubsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S3.SS3.SSS1.Px1" title="In 3.3.1 Unified Independent Space and Final Expression ‣ 3.3 Case 2: General Case with Aleatory Uncertainty in 𝐗 (X is random) ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ System-Level Uncertainty Quantification with Multiple Machine Learning Models: A Theoretical Framework" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Advantages of Transformation to Independent Standard Normal Variables</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section"><a href="#S4" title="In System-Level Uncertainty Quantification with Multiple Machine Learning Models: A Theoretical Framework" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">4 </span>GP Models</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_section">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" title="In 4 GP Models ‣ System-Level Uncertainty Quantification with Multiple Machine Learning Models: A Theoretical Framework" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Transformation to Independent Standard Normal Variables</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_paragraph">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subparagraph"><a href="#S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.SPx1" title="In Transformation to Independent Standard Normal Variables ‣ 4 GP Models ‣ System-Level Uncertainty Quantification with Multiple Machine Learning Models: A Theoretical Framework" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Step 1: Transform Correlated Gaussian Variables (<math class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>) to Independent Standard Normals (<math class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></a></li>
